<article class="bueno"><header><div class="meta case-meta"><span class="case-meta__client-full">Taco Bueno Restaurants</span><span class="case-meta__client-short">Taco Bueno</span><span class="case-meta__highlight">+147% engagement</span><span class="case-meta__role">Senior UX Strategist &amp; Creative Lead</span></div><div class="intro"><div><p>Brand Strategy &amp; Integrated Campaign UX</p><h1>Bueno<br />Means<br /><span class="heading-accent">Better.</span></h1></div><p>Brand repositioning through transparency as differentiator. 'Bueno Means Better' proved the brand's commitment to fresh-daily preparation through live streaming and user-generated content, driving 147% higher engagement and 3% check increase across pilot locations.</p></div></header>
  <CaseContents links={[{"href": "#case-section-1", "label": "Research"}, {"href": "#case-section-2", "label": "Brand platform"}, {"href": "#case-section-3", "label": "Campaign"}, {"href": "#case-section-4", "label": "Results"}]} /><figure class="hero"><img src="/images/taco_bueno_intro.webp" alt="Taco Bueno restaurant mural and interior concept" loading="eager" decoding="async" /></figure>
<section class="research" id="case-section-1" tabindex="-1"><div><p>01 / The insight</p><h2>Research &amp; Brand<br />Differentiation</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Analysis of three years of marketing revealed a consistent pattern: borrowing competitor language while falling behind. Moderated sessions with 18 current and lapsed customers across three Southwest markets showed current patrons cited freshness and made-from-scratch preparation as primary reasons for loyalty.</p><p>Lapsed customers said the brand felt interchangeable. Secondary research indicated transparency activations—showing kitchen operations rather than finished products—consistently outperformed standard promotional content in the QSR category. This insight became the strategic foundation.</p></div><figure class="research__wide"><img src="/images/taco_bueno01.webp" alt="Taco Bueno campaign system across OOH and digital" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>
<section class="proof" id="case-section-2" tabindex="-1"><div class="proof__head"><p>02 / The platform</p><h2>Freshness was the<br /><span class="heading-accent">proof point.</span></h2></div><div class="copy"><p>'Bueno Means Better' positioned the brand around one provable claim: Taco Bueno makes food fresh daily. Every campaign element demonstrated rather than asserted this claim. Voice pillars balanced humor, honesty, and appetite appeal distinctly rather than borrowing from standard playbooks.</p><p>The strategy separated Taco Bueno from competitor speed-and-value framing through sincerity as differentiator and freshness as proof point. This wasn't aspirational messaging—it was operational reality translated into brand language.</p></div><div class="proof__art"><figure><img src="/images/taco_bueno02.webp" alt="Taco Bueno storefront graphics" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><figure><img src="/images/taco_bueno03.webp" alt="Taco Bueno billboards featuring fresh food messaging" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></div></section>
<section class="digital" id="case-section-3" tabindex="-1"><div><p>03 / Show the work</p><h2>Digital UX &amp;<br />Transparency-First Campaign</h2></div><figure><img src="/images/taco_bueno04-1.webp" alt="The Bean Cam shown as a live digital billboard" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><div class="copy"><p>Website and microsite redesigns organized content around the freshness narrative. The Bean Cam—live streaming real beans being made from actual ingredients—anchored the digital experience, directly derived from research insights about kitchen visibility.</p><p>Email design employed a conversational tone matching brand voice: direct, self-aware, never corporate. The #Shellfies social campaign invited customers to share their taco experience via Snapchat, generating user-created content extending campaign reach without additional media spend.</p></div><figure class="shellfies"><img src="/images/taco_bueno05.webp" alt="Shellfies user-generated Taco Bueno social campaign" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>
<section class="results" id="case-section-4" tabindex="-1"><div><p>04 / Results</p><h2>Results &amp;<br />Market Performance</h2></div><div class="numbers"><div><b>147%</b><span>increase in social engagement</span></div><div><b>3%</b><span>increase in average check</span></div><div><b>12</b><span>pilot restaurants</span></div></div><div class="copy"><p>147% increase in social engagement across interactive ads and social activations versus prior campaign baseline. 3% increase in average check across 12 pilot restaurants during campaign period. #Shellfies drove measurable UGC volume, extending campaign reach without additional paid media.</p><p>Significant improvement in 'fresh,' 'authentic,' and 'made from scratch' perception scores across all three test markets. The campaign validated that transparency-first positioning could differentiate a legacy regional brand in a competitive QSR landscape.</p></div></section></article>
